  even open to the public and you can see  this with things like endangered species  you know when when you can grow  elephants and when you can grow salmon  and  you can grow all sorts of things you get  more of them if you can recoup some of  that so a big part of it is privatizing  the Commons and another part of it is  also working towards those few areas  understanding and gaining a real  consensus that doesn't destroy an  economy in order to save it when we're  talking about real Commons problem yeah  and let's let's not make sure that poor  people continue being poor as the  solution to our sense of guilt for our  own pollution which I think animates a  little bit too much of a sort of  Environmental Policy going going forward
 

